1. SHELL GEOMETRY
  shell  area coarse   area fine   d area     offset coarse       offset fine
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    3.0        649.0       649.8    0.11%   2.998 +/- 0.006   2.999 +/- 0.003
    4.0        844.6       845.2    0.07%   3.998 +/- 0.005   3.999 +/- 0.003
    5.0       1065.1      1065.7    0.05%   4.998 +/- 0.004   4.999 +/- 0.002

2. ACCURACY AGAINST THE ANALYTIC SURFACE
   The union-of-spheres SDF is analytic, so the true shell is exactly
   SDF = d. Discretisation error is |SDF(p) - d| for points sampled
   from each extracted mesh - measured against ground truth, not
   against the other mesh.

  shell   lattice   mean err       p95       max   (A)
--------------------------------------------------
    3.0    coarse     0.0046    0.0071    0.0790
    3.0      fine     0.0021    0.0030    0.0482
    4.0    coarse     0.0037    0.0056    0.0636
    4.0      fine     0.0017    0.0024    0.0424
    5.0    coarse     0.0032    0.0045    0.0635
    5.0      fine     0.0015    0.0020    0.0307

3. GRID OUTCOME
  sites: coarse 1448   fine 1421   difference -1.86%
  coarse: coverage mean 0.5241 p95 0.8758 A | min NN 1.0001 A
    fine: coverage mean 0.5348 p95 0.8895 A | min NN 1.0001 A

VERDICT
  worst coarse-lattice error against the analytic surface: 0.0790 A
  site spacing 1.00 A; grid resolves position to ~0.53 A
  CONVERGED - the coarse lattice reproduces the analytic surface to
  well within the site spacing, so the lattice is not limiting the grid.

############ 7. envelope justification
shells [3.0, 4.0, 5.0] A   r_min 1.0 A   density 6.0 pts/A^2   voxel 0.3 A
intended minimum standoff: 3.0 A

1. PATH CLEARANCE
   For each envelope, the standoff of its own sites measured against
   the geometries it did not include.

envelope            sites   min standoff     below floor    worst
------------------------------------------------------------------
reactant only        1402          2.345     177 (12.6%)    2.345
TS only              1415          2.533     298 (21.1%)    2.533
product only         1405          2.104     234 (16.7%)    2.104
union R+TS+P         1448              -0 (by construction)        -

2. WHICH GEOMETRY SETS THE ENVELOPE
   At each site of the union grid, which geometry is closest. If one
   dominated, the union would be unnecessary.

   reactant   binds at   730 / 1448 sites  (50.4%)
   ts         binds at   261 / 1448 sites  (18.0%)
   product    binds at   457 / 1448 sites  (31.6%)

3. SUBSTRATE MOTION ALONG THE PATH
   R -> TS   per-atom displacement: mean 0.222  max 0.617 A
   R -> P    per-atom displacement: mean 0.391  max 1.195 A

4. COST OF THE UNION
   union 1448 sites vs reactant-only 1402: +3.3% in site count
   reactant-only admits 177 sites (12.6%) that breach the 3.0 A floor later on the path
   reactant-only sites with no counterpart on the union grid (within 0.001 A): 1402 (100.0%)
   those sites stand 2.992 to 5.054 A from the reactant surface

   The union is the cheaper of the two errors: a small loss of
   candidate positions against a guarantee of path-wide clearance.
